An '''Imperial starfighter base'''<ref name="Graphic Novel" /> was located underground on the [[planet]] [[Mandalore]] and was the headquarters and base of operations of [[Moff]] [[Gideon]] and his [[Gideon's Imperial remnant|faction]] of the [[Imperial Remnant]]. Built inside a large cavern with an open entrance on the surface, the base had multiple hanger bays that held [[TIE/IN interceptor]]s and [[TIE/sa tactical bomber|TIE/sa bombers]] as well as landing pads that had [[TIE/ln space superiority starfighter]]s docked on them. The base also had a command center used by [[Moff]] [[Gideon]], a debriefing room and a [[cloning]] laboratory where the [[Force-sensitive]] [[Gideon's clones|clones]] needed for Gideon's army were produced and stored. Both the command center and the cloning laboratory could be accessed by a corridor that was blocked by four shield barriers. The base was guarded by [[Imperial Armored Commando]]s and operated by droids such as [[R-series]] [[astromech droid]]s, [[power droid]]s, and [[MSE-6 series repair droid]]s.<ref name="Chapter 23" /><ref name="Chapter 24">{{TheMandalorian|Chapter 24: The Return}}</ref>

After being [[Extraction of Moff Gideon|extracted]] from [[New Republic]] custody, [[Moff]] [[Gideon]] returned to the base. Gideon was present in the base during a meeting with the [[Shadow Council (Imperial Remnant)|Shadow Council]], in which he discussed his concerns and plans to be rid of the [[Mandalorian]]s.<ref name="Chapter 23" />

After Mandalorians returned to the planet with the goal of [[Liberation of Mandalore|retaking]] their [[homeworld]], they were ambushed and lured into the Imperial base by [[Imperial Armored Commando]]s. Gideon launched [[TIE series|TIE]] interceptors and bombers which were stationed in the base. [[Din Djarin]] was captured by Gideon, though the other Mandalorians were able to escape due to the sacrifice of [[Paz Vizsla]].<ref name="Chapter 23" />

The base was later assaulted by the remainder of the Mandalorians, inflicting heavy casualties upon the Imperial Remnant, before [[Axe Woves]] rammed [[Gideon's light cruiser|their captured]] light cruiser into the base, destroying it.<ref name="Chapter 24" />

